  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty .\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of an elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, an elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $y$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is an elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis and $a=\\frac{1}{2},\\,c=1.$",
